{"t":1793393253,"office":"LWX","station":"KDCA","point":"38.8894,-77.0352","field":"38.9429,-76.5684","field_station":"KNAK","afd":{"id":"27c3032b-98b5-4536-884f-6a0ba9b4db6c","office":"LWX","issuanceTime":"2026-10-30T17:24:00+00:00","productText":"\n000\nFXUS61 KLWX 301724\nAFDLWX\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Baltimore MD/Washington DC\n124 PM EDT Fri Oct 30 2026\n\n.WHAT HAS CHANGED...\nSmall tweaks to the wind gusts for this afternoon and lowering\ndew points for tomorrow, but otherwise forecast looks good with\nbenign conditions through the start of next week.\n\n&&\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n- 1) Precipitation chances return on Wednesday and linger\n  through the end of the week.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Precipitation chances return on Wednesday and \nlinger through the end of the week.\n\nA weak, dry cold front crossing the region earlier this morning is \nnow bringing in a much drier airmass. Mostly sunny skies this \nafternoon with breezy conditions (gusts around 20-30 mph). Winds \nquickly subside this evening as high pressure builds in from the \nnorth. Seasonable temperatures expected this weekend as highs reach \nthe 60s and lows in the 40s each day. \n\nSurface high pressure moves offshore at the start of next week, \nthough dry conditions are maintained through at least Tuesday. A \ndecaying shortwave trough aloft is now forecast to pass to our \nsouth, with likely not even a few showers in the forecast now. \nTemperatures moderate in response to the east to southeast flow with \nhighs forecast in the upper 60s to lower 70s Monday and Tuesday.\n\nThe weather pattern becomes more active beginning midweek as a deep \nupper trough approaches from the west. Global guidance shows a range \nof solutions with the commonality being multiple cut-off lows. The \nGFS has two located over central CONUS tracking along the trough. \nThe Canadian has one over central CONUS and another off the coast of \nthe Carolina's. The Euro has two over central CONUS while hinting at \nlow pressure off the coast of the Carolina's. Either way, an active \nweather pattern is expected as the trough tracks eastward through \nthe end of next week.  Precipitation chances increase on Wednesday \nwith widespread rain likely on Thursday into Thursday night. \n\nHigh temperatures will be in the upper 60s to low 70s east of the \nBlue Ridge with those along and west in the upper 50s to 60s. \nOvernight low temperatures will be in the 50s each night.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION /18Z FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nVFR conditions are expected through at least Tuesday of next week as \nhigh pressure maintains dry conditions across the region. Northwest \nwinds gust around 20-25 knots through this afternoon.\n\n&&\n\n.MARINE...\nSCA conditions are expected through tonight across the waters where \nnorthwest winds are gusting 20-25 knots. High pressure builds across \nthe region tonight through the start of next week, bringing several \ndays of favorable marine conditions.\n\n&&\n\n.LWX WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...\nDC...None.\nMD...None.\nVA...None.\nWV...None.\nMARINE...Small Craft Advisory until 9 AM EDT Saturday for ANZ530>543.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...KRR/AVS\nAVIATION...KRR\nMARINE...KRR\n"},"forecast":{"t":1793393208,"days":{"2026-10-30":{"hi":76,"lo":45,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-31":{"hi":65,"lo":45,"pop":1,"short":"Mostly Sunny"},"2026-11-01":{"hi":66,"lo":45,"pop":0,"short":"Mostly Cloudy"},"2026-11-02":{"hi":68,"lo":47,"pop":2,"short":"Partly Sunny"},"2026-11-03":{"hi":71,"lo":53,"pop":4,"short":"Mostly Sunny"},"2026-11-04":{"hi":72,"lo":59,"pop":36,"short":"Partly Sunny then Slight Chance Rain Showers"},"2026-11-05":{"hi":73,"lo":58,"pop":60,"short":"Rain Showers Likely"}}},"grid":{"t0":1793390400,"n":48,"ceil":[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,22700,20800,null,17100,21600,21600,17800,17800,17800,25000,